   $q$Which revision of sentence 11 would best conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Kobayashi's study included 240 students who all read the same science article and answered questions.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-without-analysis"},{"text":"Phones can also be helpful because students use them to check the weather and call home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"},{"text":"Phones are the main reason that students around the world struggle in every school subject.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Kobayashi's findings suggest that students who want to read with full focus should put their phones out of sight, not just on silent.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Kobayashi's findings suggest that students who want to read with full focus should put their phones out of sight, not just on silent.$q$, $q$The best conclusion draws a reasonable lesson directly from the experiment's comparison between silent phones in sight and phones out of sight. The choice about every school subject claims far more than one reading study can show.$q$, 'draft', '42e9e6fb-6d67-5df5-9790-4d353b6e41c8')
