   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence 7, best explains how the evidence in sentences 6 and 7 supports the writer's point?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Thirty-one birds a week is a large number, and nine birds a week is a smaller number.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-without-analysis"},{"text":"This proves that every bird flying over Port Winslow is now completely safe from all harm.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Volunteers in many cities enjoy spending their mornings walking and looking for wildlife.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"},{"text":"Since the weekly count dropped by more than two thirds once the towers went dark, the darker skyline appears to be protecting many birds.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Since the weekly count dropped by more than two thirds once the towers went dark, the darker skyline appears to be protecting many birds.$q$, $q$A good explanation interprets the numbers and connects them to the claim that dark towers help birds. The choice about every bird being completely safe overstates the evidence, since 9 birds a week were still harmed.$q$, 'draft', 'be021c9d-19ba-5312-9674-c15646472be0')
