  ('b0b525d5-9251-565d-b0f6-d327c0352be7', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence should the writer remove, and why?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 10, because a story about the writer's grandmother is not evidence from Kahale's poem.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence 5, because it repeats the same idea already shown by the quotation in sentence 3.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-key-evidence"},{"text":"Sentence 6, because it describes the order of the poem instead of its meaning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-key-evidence"},{"text":"Sentence 8, because it gives the writer's interpretation instead of the poet's exact words.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 10, because a story about the writer's grandmother is not evidence from Kahale's poem.$q$, $q$An analysis of a poem should use evidence from the poem, and sentence 10 is a personal detail. Sentence 5 is tempting to cut, but it adds a second patch tied to a specific memory, which builds sufficient evidence.$q$, 'draft', '5ed646ac-f522-5ec4-9ea2-1669a5d10f19')
