   $q$Which sentence should the writer delete because it does not support the analysis?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 9, because the county's orchards have nothing to do with when recess is scheduled.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence 10, because it states an opinion rather than a fact from the study.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-analysis"},{"text":"Sentence 3, because explaining how food was measured is a minor detail.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-key-evidence"},{"text":"Sentence 7, because a lunch monitor is not a trained researcher.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-key-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 9, because the county's orchards have nothing to do with when recess is scheduled.$q$, $q$Sentence 9 is an unrelated fact about the county. Sentence 10 is the writer's explanation linking the evidence to the claim, so it belongs in the draft.$q$, 'draft', '2c3ba757-29e3-50d1-9750-e68f0936d7e4')
