   $q$Which phrase best fills the blank at the start of sentence 4?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Before the tanks were installed","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-time-relationship"},{"text":"Despite collecting no rain at all","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-passage"},{"text":"By the end of the first rainy season","is_correct":true},{"text":"In contrast to the new gutters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-contrast"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By the end of the first rainy season$q$, $q$Sentence 4 reports the result after the tanks were installed in sentence 3, so a phrase showing time passing after installation fits. "Before the tanks were installed" is impossible, since the tanks could not hold water before they existed.$q$, 'draft', '3c35cde6-c7ef-58c9-a379-4f3795d988df')
