  ('3ca09cad-f154-579d-91ec-f060ca1c5f95', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Sentence 10 claims more than the evidence shows. Which revision is best supported by the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Haddad's article shows that rooftop tanks would work in most towns, no matter how much rain they receive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Haddad's article shows that Sela Verde no longer has any water problems of any kind.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Haddad's article suggests that rooftop tanks can serve a dry town well when parts are repairable locally and families know how to care for them.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Haddad's article suggests that the workshops were unnecessary once the tanks were built.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-passage"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Haddad's article suggests that rooftop tanks can serve a dry town well when parts are repairable locally and families know how to care for them.$q$, $q$The revision limits the claim to the conditions the evidence actually describes, a dry town with local repairs and trained families. The "most towns" choice still overreaches, since one town's results cannot show that tanks work regardless of rainfall.$q$, 'draft', '3c35cde6-c7ef-58c9-a379-4f3795d988df')
