  ('1998a7de-ec95-521e-8d6d-9dced7b1fa49', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence 8, best explains how the quotation supports the writer's point?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Haddad's warning shows that the tanks were only useful if families kept the water clean, which is why the workshops mattered as much as the tanks.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Haddad means that the town should stop using tanks and find a cleaner source of water instead.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-quotation"},{"text":"This quotation is the longest one in Haddad's article, so it must be the most important idea she presents.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"length-equals-strength"},{"text":"Dirty water can carry many kinds of bacteria and minerals that are harmful for people to drink.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"outside-knowledge"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Haddad's warning shows that the tanks were only useful if families kept the water clean, which is why the workshops mattered as much as the tanks.$q$, $q$The quotation explains why cleaning mattered, so the best explanation ties it to the claim that training was a key reason for success. The fact about bacteria may be true, but it relies on outside knowledge and does not connect the quotation to the writer's claim.$q$, 'draft', '3c35cde6-c7ef-58c9-a379-4f3795d988df')
